1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,543
Feel that same sting hit the same sore spot again?

2
00:00:02,863 --> 00:00:04,075
A few foods could be why.

3
00:00:04,395 --> 00:00:10,432
Zinc deficiency shows up in 28% of people with recurring sores, versus just 4% of everyone else.

4
00:00:10,752 --> 00:00:13,803
Citrus, chocolate, and coffee are the three biggest culprits.

5
00:00:14,123 --> 00:00:20,668
Citrus fruits are highly acidic and sting right on an open sore - swap them for a milder fruit like banana while it heals.

6
00:00:20,988 --> 00:00:24,117
Chocolate can trigger an allergic-type reaction in sensitive mouths.

7
00:00:24,437 --> 00:00:29,822
When you want something sweet, reach for honey instead - studies even show it can help the sore heal faster.

8
00:00:30,142 --> 00:00:35,526
Coffee's acidic too, and heavy intake is linked to more flare-ups - swap it for herbal tea instead.

9
00:00:35,846 --> 00:00:39,927
Most sores heal within a week or two - if one lingers longer, get it checked.
